# Extra browser origins allowed to call /api/*. Same-origin needs no setting.
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com,https://beta.example.com

# Trusted self-hosted deployments only. Allows private/localhost configured URLs in production.
# ALLOW_PRIVATE_PROVIDER_URLS=true

# NODE_ENV=production

# Canonical public URL used for metadata, canonical links, and structured data.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://your-branded-domain.example

# Server-side sliding-window rate limit for /api/* routes (requests per minute per API key or IP).
# RATE_LIMIT_RPM=60
# RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=true

# Public hosts: add reverse-proxy rate limiting and request-size limits before exposure.
# Never put LLM API keys in this file — users bring keys in the browser (BYOK).

# Login with ChatGPT (Experimental BETA) — signs the session cookie and encrypts
# subscription tokens at rest. For local/single-node, ai.diy persists a generated
# secret in .data/lwc-secret so sessions survive npm start restarts.
# Serverless production MUST set a stable shared secret:
# LWC_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# Vercel/Upstash Redis REST credentials make sessions survive cold starts and
# span multiple function instances. KV_REST_API_* aliases are also accepted.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<database>.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# Optional Codex CLI client_version — ChatGPT gates the model catalog on this.
# Defaults to a current Codex release (0.147.0). Bump if models disappear.
# LWC_CLIENT_VERSION=0.147.0

# Authenticated sessions default to 180 days and renew while used (range: 1-365).
# LWC_SESSION_DAYS=180

# Multi-instance / serverless hosts also need a shared session store (Redis/KV).
# The bundled file store is single-node only (Docker one replica / local).

# Vercel Connect (Optional, Beta) — app-scoped tokens for MCP servers and the
# connect_request tool. On Vercel, tokens are injected automatically (OIDC).
# Self-hosted instances authenticate with a Vercel access token instead:
# VERCEL_TOKEN=xxx

# Local dev/self-host quick start: `vercel link` once, then `vercel env pull`
# writes .env.local (with a short-lived dev VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN when Connect is
# enabled) and the production server loads .env* automatically.
# Long-running local instances should set VERCEL_TOKEN above instead.

# Connectors are declared as CONNECT_CONNECTOR_<KEY>=<connector id or UID>.
# Each may optionally carry an API base URL (for connect_request calls) and
# space-separated app scopes (defaults to the connector's app scopes):
# CONNECT_CONNECTOR_GITHUB=scl_xxx
# CONNECT_BASE_URL_GITHUB=https://api.github.com
# CONNECT_SCOPES_GITHUB=
